# C++ style

New C++ follows the [Google C++ Style Guide](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html). Formatting is `.clang-format` (`BasedOnStyle: Google`). Lint is `.clang-tidy` (`google-*` plus Google naming).

- Target C++17. New translation units are `.cc`; headers are `.h`. Filenames are lowercase with underscores.
- Types, functions, and enums are `PascalCase`. Enumerators and static constants are `kPascalCase`. Variables and parameters are `snake_case`. Class data members end in `_`. Namespaces are lowercase. Macros are `UPPER_SNAKE` with a project prefix.
- Braces on the same line. Pointers and references bind left (`int* p`). Prefer `using` over `typedef`, `nullptr` over `NULL` or `0`, and `override` on virtual overrides.
- No `using namespace` in headers. Constructors callable with one argument are `explicit`. Include the headers you use.

The existing decimal C API is an exception: keep `bid_*` functions and `BID_` / `DEC_` / `DPML_` macros. Do not rename them and do not run clang-format across unmodified BID sources.

```cpp
// Good
class DecimalStatus {
 public:
  int flag_count() const { return flag_count_; }

 private:
  int flag_count_ = 0;
};
```
